course: dictionary
lesson: 11975
title: Words of joy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you the mood of a whole event. Celebratory is one of them. Its root is celebrate, which means to mark something happy, and the ending -ory shows it describes something, such as a cake or a meal.
explain: «The family had a celebratory meal after the football match.» The clues are after the match: people often eat together when something good has happened, like a win. So celebratory means done to celebrate something happy. Test it: put "happy" in place of the word and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The room had a celebratory mood, with balloons and music.» Balloons and music are clues too. The words around a new word often tell you its feeling even when you do not know the word yet.
fact: Celebratory means done or made to celebrate something happy, like a birthday or a win.
fact: Celebratory is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as a cake, a dance or a meal.
fact: Phrases you may meet are celebratory meal, celebratory mood and celebratory drink.
fact: «A celebratory dance» shows that people are joyful about something good.
fact: Celebratory comes from celebrate, so remember celebrate first and the meaning follows.
exercise: «Everyone wore party hats at the celebratory picnic.» What does celebratory mean? | Done in a hurry | Very cold and wet | *Done to celebrate something happy | Sad and quiet
exercise: «The room had a celebratory mood, with balloons and music.» What kind of mood is it? | A mood for a long, quiet sleep | A worried mood | A cold, grey mood | *A joyful mood, for something good
exercise: Maya says, «A celebratory drink is a drink for a sad day.» Is she right? | *No, it is a drink made to celebrate something happy | No, it is a drink for a long walk | Yes, it is for a sad day | Yes, because it is a cold drink
test: «She made a celebratory cake when her dog won the show.» What does celebratory mean here? | Made very quickly for a sad day | Made by mistake | *Made to celebrate something happy | Made of stone
test: In «The team had a celebratory meal after the win», which words are the best clue to the meaning? | The team | meal | *after the win | had a
exam: Ayo says, «Celebratory means sad and quiet.» Is Ayo right? | Yes, because celebrate means sad | Only on a birthday | *No, it means done to celebrate something happy | Yes, because it is a quiet word
